262 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 194 0 R
/T (         The overall design of this robot is the result of careful consideration for how it would ultimately be programmed. As students, we found that going into this project, we all needed the greatest improvement in the field of programming. Knowing that we had to deliver the final project within just a few short weeks, many of the decisions we made were to simplify the motion of the robot as much as possible, while still retaining the capability to traverse and harvest fruit from any field position. Our mechanisms were all designed with the goal of making our late stage programming as simple as possible by limiting the ranges of motion to the minimum number possible, adding physical sensors to limit motion, and)
